# About Allen

![Allen](/img/avatar.jpg)

Allen is a native Chinese speaker who teaches Chinese and Tai Chi to learners outside China, in clear English, at a slow pace.

His approach is simple: start with a real scene, give you a real sentence, explain why Chinese people say it that way, and then let you practise it. Culture is not an extra chapter at the end — it is the reason the sentence sounds the way it does. Tai Chi follows the same idea: one movement at a time, slowly, until it feels natural.

> Full introduction, teaching background, and a longer bilingual introduction will be added here. This page is intentionally short at launch, rather than filled with claims that are not yet written. Tai Chi style, form, and class format will also be added here once Allen confirms them.

## What you will learn here

- Chinese you can actually say, not only read in a textbook
- Why a direct translation often sounds wrong, and what sounds natural instead
- Chinese culture through language: greetings, food, family, festivals, and daily life
- Tai Chi, one movement at a time — and the Chinese words that go with it
- China news, explained in plain English, with the words you need to follow it

